0	section	Starting the quest
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Kaqemeex	What brings you to our holy monument?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Who are you?
2	line	Player	Who are you?
2	line	Kaqemeex	We are the druids of Guthix. We worship our god at our famous stone circles. You will find them located throughout these lands.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	What about the stone circle full of dark wizards?
3	line	Player	What about the stone circle full of dark wizards?
3	line	Kaqemeex	That used to be OUR stone circle. Unfortunately, many many years ago, dark wizards cast a wicked spell upon it so that they could corrupt its power for their own evil ends.
3	line	Kaqemeex	When they cursed the rocks for their rituals they made them useless to us and our magics. We require a brave adventurer to go on a quest for us to help purify the circle of Varrock.
3	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that your combat level is lower than the recommended level of 10.
3	select	Start the Druidic Ritual quest?
3	option	Yes.
4	action	below
3	option	No.
4	action	below
2	option	So what's so good about Guthix?
3	line	Player	So what's so good about Guthix?
3	line	Kaqemeex	Guthix is the oldest and most powerful god in Gielinor. His existence is vital to this world. He is the god of balance, and nature; he is also a very part of this world.
3	line	Kaqemeex	He exists in the trees, and the flowers, the water and the rocks. He is everywhere. His purpose is to ensure balance in everything in this world, and as such we worship him.
3	line	Player	He sounds kind of boring...
3	line	Kaqemeex	Some day when your mind achieves enlightenment you will see the true beauty of his power.
3	action	end
2	option	Well, I'll be on my way now.
3	line	Player	Well, I'll be on my way now.
3	line	Kaqemeex	Goodbye adventurer. I feel we shall meet again.
3	action	end
1	option	I'm in search of a quest.
2	line	Player	I'm in search of a quest.
2	line	Kaqemeex	Hmm. I think I may have a worthwhile quest for you actually. I don't know if you are familiar with the stone circle south of Varrock or not, but...
2	line	Kaqemeex	That used to be OUR stone circle. Unfortunately, many many years ago, dark wizards cast a wicked spell upon it so that they could corrupt its power for their own evil ends.
2	line	Kaqemeex	When they cursed the rocks for their rituals they made them useless to us and our magics. We require a brave adventurer to go on a quest for us to help purify the circle of Varrock.
2	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that your combat level is lower than the recommended level of 10.
2	select	Start the Druidic Ritual quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	Okay, I will try and help.
3	line	Kaqemeex	Excellent. Go to the village south of this place and speak to my fellow druid, Sanfew, who is working on the purification ritual. He knows what is required to complete it.
3	line	Player	Will do.
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	No, that doesn't sound very interesting.
3	line	Kaqemeex	I will not try and change your mind adventurer. Some day when you have matured you may reconsider your position. We will wait until then.
3	action	end
1	option	Did you build this?
2	line	Player	Did you build this?
2	line	Kaqemeex	What, personally? No, of course I didn't. However, our forefathers did. The first Druids of Guthix built many stone circles across these lands over eight hundred years ago.
2	line	Kaqemeex	Unfortunately we only know of two remaining, and of those only one is usable by us anymore.
